// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 08-alias-validity
// facility: rule.value-object.write [Write-Conflict]; spec/08 §4 [Standing-Local] H3 (an argument arrives clash-free, D-0219, CHG-0258); conf.reference-passed-on-while-reborrowed
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.aliasing-conflict (dynamic)
//
// An existing exclusive reference is passed on whole while a shared
// reborrow of it lives. Passing it forms no borrow, so nothing is checked
// at the call; the callee's write through it meets the live shared path
// and faults. `cobc` once ran such a call through its direct body, whose
// accesses are unchecked, with no arrival test while the thread was
// alone: the write went through and the shared reference saw `x` change
// while it lived. Found by the model (`impl/model`, D-0219).

import std;

fn bump(ref<i32, exclusive> p)
{
    *p = *p + 1;
}

fn main()
{
    i32 x = 1;
    auto r = &mut x;
    auto s = &*r;
    i32 before = *s;
    bump(r);
    printf("%v %v\n", before, *s);
}
